[36m(RolloutExecutor pid=36454)[0m # Description
[36m(RolloutExecutor pid=36454)[0m 
[36m(RolloutExecutor pid=36454)[0m `caplog.get_records()` gets decoupled from actual caplog records when `caplog.clear()` is called. As a result, after `caplog.clear()` is called, `caplog.get_records()` is frozen: it does not get cleared, nor does it get new records.
[36m(RolloutExecutor pid=36454)[0m 
[36m(RolloutExecutor pid=36454)[0m During test set up it is [set to the same list](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/blob/28e8c8582ea947704655a3c3f2d57184831336fd/src/_pytest/logging.py#L699) as `caplog.records`, but the latter gets [replaced rather than cleared](https://github.com/pytest-dev/pytest/blob/28e8c8582ea947704655a3c3f2d57184831336fd/src/_pytest/logging.py#L345) in `caplog.clear()`, which diverges the two objects.
[36m(RolloutExecutor pid=36454)[0m 
